/// A type name written in a case other than the built-in spelling.
///
/// The asymmetry is the point here.  The type name operand of 'is' is already
/// folded by both processors, so 'X is integer' is true; the same name in an
/// annotation is compared exactly, so 'var X : integer' is rejected.  One
/// position folds and the other does not.
///
/// Like CaseEnumMember this aborts the file during checking rather than failing
/// a test, so it needs a file of its own.
///
/// Fails with: Uncaught: Type mismatch!  (no tests run)
///
test 'A type name in an annotation resolves through any spelling';
begin
    var Counted : integer := 1;

    AssertTrue (Counted is Integer);
    AssertEqual (1, Counted);
end
